{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600136",
      "title": "How Redux Works",
      "sourceHash": "df4bcca4fda93ab661cf809a07a6aa92316d38e6eb31adacd8ce160cc75c4d87",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.87,
          "en": "So now that we know what Redux is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.87,
          "end": 8.22,
          "en": "basically an alternative to react context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.22,
          "end": 11.52,
          "en": "and now that we also know why we might wanna use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.52,
          "end": 14.64,
          "en": "over react context in some apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.64,
          "end": 16.67,
          "en": "the big question that remains,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.67,
          "end": 19.66,
          "en": "is how does Redux work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.66,
          "end": 21.5,
          "en": "Well, Redux is all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.5,
          "end": 24.97,
          "en": "about having one Central Data Store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.97,
          "end": 27.12,
          "en": "in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.12,
          "end": 29.15,
          "en": "And with data I mean state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.15,
          "end": 30.85,
          "en": "And that is super important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.85,
          "end": 33.27,
          "en": "You have exactly one store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.27,
          "end": 36.1,
          "en": "You never have more than one store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.1,
          "end": 37.56,
          "en": "It's one store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.56,
          "end": 41.47,
          "en": "for all your state for your entire application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.47,
          "end": 43.21,
          "en": "So in this store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.21,
          "end": 46.69,
          "en": "you would store authentication state theming,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.69,
          "end": 49.1,
          "en": "maybe some user input state you wanna save,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.1,
          "end": 50.41,
          "en": "whatever it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.41,
          "end": 53.93,
          "en": "Whichever cross component or app wide state you have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.93,
          "end": 56.32,
          "en": "it goes into this one store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.32,
          "end": 58.786,
          "en": "Now this might sound unmaintainable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 58.786,
          "end": 60.35,
          "en": "but the good thing is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.35,
          "end": 63.02,
          "en": "that we don't directly need to manage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 63.02,
          "end": 65.13,
          "en": "the entire store all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 65.13,
          "end": 69.25,
          "en": "As you will see from this module and the next modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.25,
          "end": 71.81,
          "en": "So we have this Central Data Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 71.81,
          "end": 73.23,
          "en": "What do we do with it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 73.23,
          "end": 76.1,
          "en": "Ultimately, we have data in that store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 76.1,
          "end": 79.8,
          "en": "so that we can use it from inside our components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.8,
          "end": 82.39,
          "en": "Because if some data there changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 82.39,
          "end": 85.45,
          "en": "if the authentication status of a user changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 85.45,
          "end": 89.18,
          "en": "for example, we wanna know about that in a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 89.18,
          "end": 91.15,
          "en": "so that we can react accordingly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 91.15,
          "end": 92.423,
          "en": "and update the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 93.32,
          "end": 97.09,
          "en": "For this components set up subscriptions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.09,
          "end": 99.61,
          "en": "to our Central Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.61,
          "end": 101.43,
          "en": "They subscribe to the store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.43,
          "end": 103.27000000000001,
          "en": "and whenever the data changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.27000000000001,
          "end": 105.64,
          "en": "the store notifies components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 105.64,
          "end": 109.07,
          "en": "and then components can get the data they need,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 109.07,
          "end": 112.2,
          "en": "for example the current authentication status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 112.2,
          "end": 115.56,
          "en": "so they get a slice of the Redux store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 115.56,
          "end": 117.43,
          "en": "and they can then use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 117.43,
          "end": 119.50999999999999,
          "en": "And of course we're going to see all of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 119.50999999999999,
          "end": 122.543,
          "en": "in action, in detail, in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 123.47,
          "end": 126.15,
          "en": "So that's how we get data out of the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.15,
          "end": 126.983,
          "en": "But of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 126.983,
          "end": 128.63,
          "en": "since this is state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 128.63,
          "end": 132,
          "en": "so data which also changes from time to time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 132,
          "end": 134.9,
          "en": "We need a way of changing that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 134.9,
          "end": 137.97,
          "en": "So how do we change data into stored in?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 137.97,
          "end": 139.85,
          "en": "Here's one very important rule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 139.85,
          "end": 143.05,
          "en": "Components, never important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 143.05,
          "end": 147.87,
          "en": "Never, directly manipulate the store data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 147.87,
          "end": 149.67000000000002,
          "en": "So we have that subscription,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 149.67000000000002,
          "end": 153.05,
          "en": "but we don't have a data flow in the other direction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 153.05,
          "end": 155.86,
          "en": "At least not a direct data flow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 155.86,
          "end": 160.053,
          "en": "Components don't directly manipulate that data in the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 161.04,
          "end": 164.97,
          "en": "Instead for debt, we use a concept called reducers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 164.97,
          "end": 167.93,
          "en": "We have a reducer function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 167.93,
          "end": 171.01,
          "en": "This reducer function which we have to set up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 171.01,
          "end": 174.72,
          "en": "This function is responsible, for mutating.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 174.72,
          "end": 177.61,
          "en": "So for changing the store data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 177.61,
          "end": 179.45,
          "en": "Now One important note here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 179.45,
          "end": 181.17,
          "en": "the term reducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 181.17,
          "end": 183.89,
          "en": "is of course something we have heard before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 183.89,
          "end": 188.073,
          "en": "with use reducer and the reducer function here is not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 188.073,
          "end": 191.34,
          "en": "that use reducer hook we learned about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 191.34,
          "end": 196.34,
          "en": "Reducer functions in general, are just a general concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 196.77,
          "end": 200.87,
          "en": "Reducer functions are functions, which takes some input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 200.87,
          "end": 203.3,
          "en": "and then transform that input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 203.3,
          "end": 205.04,
          "en": "they reduce it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 205.04,
          "end": 208.51,
          "en": "for example they can reduce a list of numbers to the sum",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 208.51,
          "end": 211.32999999999998,
          "en": "of that number and that's just one example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 211.32999999999998,
          "end": 214.57,
          "en": "But they in general transform, inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 214.57,
          "end": 217.75,
          "en": "and spit out a new output a new result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 217.75,
          "end": 220.35,
          "en": "So that's a general programming concept,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 220.35,
          "end": 222.63,
          "en": "which use reducer, does hook uses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 222.63,
          "end": 226.993,
          "en": "and which this reducer function Redux will use also uses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 228.03,
          "end": 229.87,
          "en": "Okay so we have a reducer function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 229.87,
          "end": 233.74,
          "en": "which is responsible for updating the store data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 233.74,
          "end": 237.3,
          "en": "And we have components that subscribe to that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 237.3,
          "end": 241.41,
          "en": "How do we now connect components and that reducer function?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 241.41,
          "end": 242.84,
          "en": "Because ultimately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 242.84,
          "end": 245.3,
          "en": "it will of course be the components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 245.3,
          "end": 248.16,
          "en": "that should trigger a data change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 248.16,
          "end": 251.23,
          "en": "It is for example a click on a button in a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 251.23,
          "end": 254.05,
          "en": "that should trigger some data change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 254.05,
          "end": 255.563,
          "en": "So how do we connect that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 256.4,
          "end": 258.96,
          "en": "Trigger is a good word for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 258.96,
          "end": 261.37,
          "en": "Because we have a third concept here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 261.37,
          "end": 266.37,
          "en": "We have actions and components dispatch actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 266.4,
          "end": 267.96,
          "en": "And therefore we could also say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 267.96,
          "end": 271.67,
          "en": "that components trigger, certain actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 271.67,
          "end": 275.97,
          "en": "Now an action is really just a simple JavaScript object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 275.97,
          "end": 278.74,
          "en": "which describes the kind of operation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 278.74,
          "end": 281.40999999999997,
          "en": "the reducers should perform.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 281.40999999999997,
          "end": 285.77,
          "en": "Therefore, Redux then forwards actions to the reducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 285.77,
          "end": 289.98,
          "en": "reads that description of the desired operation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 289.98,
          "end": 291.4,
          "en": "if you wanna to call it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 291.4,
          "end": 296.06,
          "en": "and then this operation is performed by the reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 296.06,
          "end": 298.59000000000003,
          "en": "So components dispatch actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 298.59000000000003,
          "end": 300.77,
          "en": "which describe what should be done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 300.77,
          "end": 302.77,
          "en": "but don't do it directly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 302.77,
          "end": 305.94,
          "en": "then these actions are forwarded to the reducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 305.94,
          "end": 308.8,
          "en": "the reducer then does what the action wants,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 308.8,
          "end": 310.05,
          "en": "the reducer to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 310.05,
          "end": 313.97,
          "en": "And then the reducer, spits out a new state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 313.97,
          "end": 317.98,
          "en": "which effectively will replace the existing state in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 317.98,
          "end": 319.97,
          "en": "that Central Data Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 319.97,
          "end": 321.56,
          "en": "And when that happens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 321.56,
          "end": 324.56,
          "en": "when that state in that data store is updated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 324.56,
          "end": 327.58,
          "en": "subscribing components are notified,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 327.58,
          "end": 329.723,
          "en": "so that they can update their UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 331.34,
          "end": 334.08,
          "en": "That's how Redux works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 334.08,
          "end": 335.75,
          "en": "Now of course that's all nice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 335.75,
          "end": 337.55,
          "en": "That's great theory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 337.55,
          "end": 341.22,
          "en": "But how does that look like in reality then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 341.22,
          "end": 344.45,
          "en": "How does the code we have to write look like?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 344.45,
          "end": 346.65,
          "en": "Well that's what we're going to explore now.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}